Let $B$ be the bit sent and $r = (1, 1, 0)$ the received sequence. From the data:

- $P(\text{receive } 1 \mid B = 1) = 0.8$ and $P(\text{receive } 0 \mid B = 1) = 0.2$;
- $P(\text{receive } 1 \mid B = 0) = 0.1$ and $P(\text{receive } 0 \mid B = 0) = 0.9$;
- prior: $P(B = 1) = 0.4$ and $P(B = 0) = 0.6$.
